# The Postman collection ships with working credentials so it runs on import
# without a single edit. That is the point of it, and also why it must not be
# committed — git history keeps a password long after the file is deleted.
# docs/api/README.md documents the same API and carries none.
docs/api/*.postman_collection.json

# The Scopus exports the review was built against: 5.7 MB of real data, and the
# csv carries a Correspondence Address column, so it is 1,572 rows of named
# people with their email addresses. Two reasons it stays out: git history keeps
# them forever, and this directory is under public/, where anything committed is
# downloadable by anyone who guesses the filename. Uploads belong in
# storage/app/private/scopus, which the review already writes to and which is
# already ignored.
public/documents/scopas/
